Subject: [PATCH] gbp_agent: re-bind the notify-vrf RPC consumer

Upstream commit 3be1e3c "Add RPCs for distributed SNAT" replaced the
notify-vrf consumer with notify-snat instead of adding alongside it, so
the agent no longer subscribes to a fanout topic our neutron-server still
casts on. Everything else survives, which is what makes it a slip rather
than a removal:

  * the constant           opflexagent/rpc.py:25   NOTIFY_VRF = 'notify-vrf'
  * the server-side cast   opflexagent/rpc.py:48   topic_opflex_notify_vrf
                           opflexagent/rpc.py:75   cast 'opflex_notify_vrf'
  * the agent-side handler opflexagent/rpc.py:357  OpenstackRpcMixin.
                                                   opflex_notify_vrf()

Only the queue binding is gone. GBPOpflexAgent mixes in OpenstackRpcMixin
(gbp_agent.py:63-64), so the handler is present on the agent and this
one-line restoration is sufficient - nothing else has to change.

Without it, apic_aim's VRF and address-scope notifications are cast into a
queue nothing consumes and the compute's VRF file goes stale silently:
ports still bind, so the failure surfaces later as traffic that does not
route. There is no natural fallback. The subnet_update consumer looks like
partial cover, but it adds subnet['tenant_id'] to self.updated_vrf while
the vrf_dict it is intersected against is keyed on 'tenant_name vrf_name'
strings, so it never matches.

Present on stable/2025.1, stable/2025.2, stable/2026.1 and master, so no
choice of upstream branch avoids it. Reported to noironetworks; drop this
patch at the next pin bump if it is fixed upstream.

--- var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/opflexagent/gbp_agent.py
+++ var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/opflexagent/gbp_agent.py
@@ -210,6 +210,7 @@
                      [topics.PORT, topics.DELETE],
                      [topics.SECURITY_GROUP, topics.UPDATE],
                      [topics.SUBNET, topics.UPDATE],
+                     [rpc.TOPIC_OPFLEX, rpc.NOTIFY_VRF, topics.UPDATE],
                      [rpc.TOPIC_OPFLEX, rpc.NOTIFY_SNAT, topics.UPDATE],
                      [rpc.TOPIC_OPFLEX, rpc.VRF, topics.UPDATE],
                      [rpc.TOPIC_OPFLEX, rpc.SNAT, topics.UPDATE]]
